{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3111","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3111","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3111\",\"parent_revision\":\"e9d498d96e2eaea1e25a31b3ed7840e2c15acf4fa9592d94db8076685c35bdbe\",\"root_revision\":\"e9d498d96e2eaea1e25a31b3ed7840e2c15acf4fa9592d94db8076685c35bdbe\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: Ideas\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-21\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThis is an exploration/experiment item (deliverable = experiment result or design decision with evidence, not a shipped feature). Part of the graph-engineering exploration set (#3097-#3110). Shared design constraint: the model writes judgment once as typed planning-time data; existing machinery applies it deterministically; no new scheduler or generic graph runtime.\\n\\nWhat/why: The plugin-creator:ensemble-rule-review skill codifies a fan-out map-reduce pattern for rule-following work: partition a 10+ criterion ruleset across parallel rigid cheap workers with deliberately overlapping slices, collect findings in a fixed candidate schema, and corroboration-weight the merge (deterministic bookend scripts plan_ensemble.py and reduce.py around the only fuzzy step). User-reported results in this repo: haiku worker ensembles following this process are faster AND cheaper than a single sonnet pass with no quality loss for checklist-shaped, small-attention-focus task types (the skill records ~35x speedup at comparable recall on a journal-review case). DH's dispatch model does not know this pattern exists: every task routes to a single task-worker regardless of task shape, so checklist-shaped work pays single-capable-agent prices and suffers the exact attention-degradation failure the ensemble skill exists to solve (silent rule drops as ruleset size grows).\\n\\nMitigates: overpaying capable-tier prices for mechanical rule-checking; silent criterion drops in single-pass rubric application; the multi-perspective-review gap the ensemble skill itself documents (its prior-art section names dh multi-perspective-review as a partial implementation missing the fixed candidate schema and the corroboration-weight reducer \u2014 it merges by any-REJECT).\\n\\nBenefit lands in: quality-gate and audit cost (cheap-tier fleets where the design has removed inference from the worker's job); review coverage (overlap denoises attention variance); and the complexity-scoring routing decision (#3097).\\n\\nProposed exploration: (1) add a task SHAPE axis to the #3097 complexity metadata \u2014 mechanical-checklist vs judgment \u2014 because shape decides ensemble-vs-single-worker routing while size decides tier and decomposition; (2) define the dispatch-loop routing rule: checklist-shaped tasks above N criteria route to an ensemble dispatch (plan_ensemble.py assignment -> rigid workers x N -> reduce.py) instead of a single task-worker; (3) upgrade multi-perspective-review with the two pieces the ensemble skill says it lacks (fixed candidate schema, corroboration reducer), as the reference integration; (4) compose with refute-framed verification (#3107): ensemble supplies recall, an independent different-family verifier supplies precision \u2014 the ensemble skill is explicit that corroboration boosts shared-model bias rather than cancelling it, so the verifier must not share the workers' model family; (5) resolve the placement design question: the pattern lives in the plugin-creator plugin while DH would consume it, and plugins are standalone products that must not reference each other's internals \u2014 decide between promoting the pattern (scripts + worker contract) into DH's own machinery vs defining a sanctioned cross-plugin dependency; (6) measure per the harness success metric: same-or-better completion and compliance, fewer turns and fewer tokens, against a single-sonnet-pass baseline on one real checklist-shaped step.\\n\\nRelated: #3097 (shape axis is a refinement of its score design \u2014 hard composition); #3103 (review-depth routing is a sibling routing rule); #3107 (verifier composition); plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/SKILL.md (the pattern source, including its conversion-workflow and orchestrator-playbook references); plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review (reference integration target).\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **explore ensemble fan-out as a first-class dh dispatch pattern for checklist-shaped work** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: graph-engineering exploration set + ensemble-rule-review skill (user-reported cost/quality results)\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"965ebc9aed7f1bcba4ea74fd18bc1cf1cfc2eb06eabcbe531f97495923ed08d0\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQIo2NA\"}"}